# Working copies and throwaway config dirs are large and machine-specific. Rows
# ARE committed — they are the evidence the write-ups cite, and rows-regraded/
# carries `regradedFrom` so any oracle correction stays auditable. Representative
# transcripts are committed under probes/*/transcripts/ as oracle regression
# fixtures; the full per-trial stream-json is not.
#
# Exception: the `rule-drift` arm A transcripts from the 2026-08-11 Fable 5
# contrast (1.6 MB). The M1 mechanism claim IS a string match over those files
# — `doc-read` := transcript contains `CONVENTIONS.md` — so a reader who cannot
# read them cannot check the repository's strongest result. `mechanism.tsv` in
# each run dir is the derived table; these are what it derives from.
# (The pattern is `transcripts/*`, not `transcripts/`: git will not descend into
# an excluded directory, so a negation inside one never matches.)
evals/runs/*/trials/
evals/runs/*/transcripts/*
!evals/runs/contrast-rule-drift-fable5/transcripts/rule-drift-A-*.jsonl
!evals/runs/gate-log-redaction-fable5/transcripts/*
evals/runs/*/cfg/
evals/runs/smoke*/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
